{/*
  RULES FOR ELEMENTS THE SCRIPT BUILDS.

  Astro scopes a component's styles by appending a [data-astro-cid-…] attribute
  to both the selectors and the elements in its template. Elements created with
  document.createElement never get that attribute, so a scoped rule cannot match
  one - silently. Every row of the posts table is built in script, and every one
  of these rules had therefore been dead: `.icon-btn` was resolving to a 16px
  bare glyph rather than a 38px button, and the photo count was left-aligned in
  a column whose header said centred.

  The column widths looked right only because the <th> in the template carries
  them and a table propagates column width from its header.

  So these are global, and scoped by hand to `.admin` instead - a class that IS
  in the template, which keeps them off the rest of the site.
*/}
<style is:global>
  :is(.admin, .sheet) .btn {
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem;
